  "predicted_delta_text": "**PREDICTION**:  \n`s11_db improves by ~3 dB` \u2014 replacing the resistor R2 with a **capacitor C3 to ground** at the source node (n3) **removes the resistive degeneration** and instead provides **AC grounding** of the source. This **reduces the source impedance seen at RF**, which improves input impedance matching. The capacitor **shunts the source to ground at RF**, effectively **removing the source degeneration effect** that was degrading S11, while still allowing DC bias. This is a **common trick in LNA design to improve input match**.\n\n---",
